From 6f5ff19b1bd3e9625d89b09d88f810e90055077b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:20:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/18] Opening: resume the film after a window switch instead
 of freezing on it

A hidden or frozen tab can pause the opening film and the browser does not
always resume it, so returning left the page stuck on the paused film (the
clip never ended, so the World was never revealed). On visibilitychange,
document resume, pageshow and focus the film now resumes once (muted retry
on refusal); a film that already ended enters directly, and one that still
does not move within 3 s hands over to the normal "preparing the world" wait.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
